sec.p:
To quantify the cross-correlation between elongation rate ER(t) and flagellar activity A(t), we first subtracted the mean from each time series ER′(t) = ER(t) − ⟨ER⟩, A′(t) = A(t) − ⟨A⟩, and then used the function ‘correlate’ from the SciPy library in Python. The normalized cross-correlation is defined as
CorrER,A(lag)=∑tER′(t)A′(t+lag)(∑tER′(t)2)(∑tA′(t)2), \begin{document}$$\displaystyle )=\frac{\sum_{t} E R^{\prime}(t) A^{\prime}(t+\text { lag })}{\sqrt{\left(\sum_{t} E R^{\prime}(t)^{2}\right)\left(\sum_{t} A^{\prime}(t)^{2}\right)}}$$\end{document}
where l is the time lag. In practice, we evaluated the numerator using ‘correlate’ function from SciPy library in Python and normalized by the square root of the product of the zero-lag autocorrelations, by using the same function.
